  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, so we have no information about whether scvi_n200 or pca_n2000 could outperform it. The best result so far is config_007 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542), and weighted fusion with imagenet_vit_l appears to be the strongest image-side combination. Question: Does replacing scgpt with scvi_n200 (a learned generative RNA encoder) while keeping the best image encoder and fusion improve accuracy? This is the most important unexplored axis—RNA encoder choice—since it could reveal a fundamentally better representation. Why this experiment: It directly extends the best-performing configuration by swapping only the RNA encoder, isolating that variable. It also has moderate expected cost (~3–4 GPU hours, comparable to config_007's 2.94 h since both use a learned RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l and avgpool), making it an efficient use of the remaining 6 experiments to reduce uncertainty about the RNA encoder before committing to further aggregation or profile-setting variations."
}

